summary:
- topic: Robotics Team Recognition
  text: The South Portland High School robotics team was recognized for their achievement
    in reaching the world championships, including a robot demonstration and student
    presentations. Board members praised the team's technical skills, teamwork, and
    representation of the district.
- topic: Superintendent's Report and Enrollment Update
  text: The Superintendent's report acknowledged food service staff for their vital
    role and provided an update on student enrollment, which has leveled out but is
    anticipated to decrease slightly next year due to graduating seniors and a smaller
    incoming kindergarten class.
- topic: FY24 Audit Findings and Corrective Actions
  text: An in-depth presentation on the FY24 audit revealed findings related to cash
    procedures at the high school, payroll processes, grant reconciliation, and budget
    overspending. The administration outlined steps taken and planned, including increased
    training, monthly reconciliations, and a budget freeze, to address these issues
    and improve financial management.
- topic: High School Performance Data
  text: The SPHS Principal reported positive trends in student attendance, a significant
    decrease in out-of-school suspensions due to PBIS implementation, and academic
    growth reflected in improved SAT scores and the piloting of NWEA pre/post assessments
    in math.
- topic: Personnel Decisions and Notable Retirement
  text: The consent agenda, including various donations and numerous personnel appointments
    (second probationary and first continuing contracts), was approved. The board
    also paid special tribute to Craig Uffington, the SPHS band director, who is retiring
    after 30 years of significant impact on students and music education.
- topic: Public Comment on Teacher Non-Renewals
  text: Several citizens and teachers expressed strong concerns during public comment
    regarding the non-renewal of contracts for two pre-K special education teachers.
    Speakers praised their expertise, dedication, and critical role in supporting
    vulnerable students, questioning the district's decision and calling for reconsideration.
- topic: Policy Updates and Board Requests
  text: The board approved policy updates for the superintendent's job description.
    A vote on the concussion policy was postponed for further clarification on parental
    approval for return-to-play. Board members also requested DEI training and a workshop
    on future budget processes.
